// Verification half of the detection-plane record_integrity lane: read
// the last 24h of every core-node ocsf class back, recompute each
// record's attestation fingerprint over the canonical serialization,
// and walk the per-node prev_event chain; a Detection Finding (2004)
// drops for every break (content tamper, deletion, splice).
//
// SCHEDULED, hourly — the every wrapper, the loader-pipeline shape
// (opencti-osint-loader / fleet-assets-loader): the first walk fires at
// pipeline start (the previous startup-once behavior, preserved) and
// every 1h re-walks the rolling 24h window. every waits for a running
// walk before starting the next (no concurrent walks against the
// store); restart-on-error still relaunches the pipeline on a hard
// failure.
//
// TWO legs out per break (docs/issues/
// tenzir-record-integrity-attestations.md, the scheduled-walk box):
// - stdout: the raw finding as the operator mints it — pod-log
//   visibility, unchanged.
// - ocsf.Detection_Finding: the finding rides ocsf_derive + ocsf_cast
//   into the lake's class shape and INSERTs with the tenzir user —
//   the same table the Grafana tenzir-findings rule reads
//   (03-services/observability/grafana/alerting/tenzir-findings.yaml):
//   class_uid 2004 + severity 4 land inside the rule's WHERE clauses,
//   so a break pages through the agent_invoke bridge (homelab-agent
//   -> the investigator) instead of waiting for a human to read pod
//   logs. The package test detection-verify-finding pins the shape
//   against the rule's SQL. Tamper evidence is append-only: while a
//   break persists, each hourly walk re-emits its finding and the rule
//   re-fires — re-paging until the tamper is remediated, the honest
//   loop for evidence nobody can "acknowledge away". The written
//   findings carry no attestation (the chain covers archive-rule
//   writes, and these rows bypass the archive rule); later walks read
//   them back and skip them as pre-epoch rows — the lane never
//   self-feeds.
//
// The read-back is windowed (24h) because the walk sorts the merged
// stream in memory: a full-table walk over 22M+ archived rows would
// buffer gigabytes against the node's 8Gi limit. The per-class
// from_clickhouse reads are table mode (the vendor's catch-all
// reconstruction — the per-class tables split each record across typed
// columns + the event JSON, and only table mode reverses that split),
// merged into ONE stream because the per-node chain crosses classes,
// with the window filter inside each branch so ClickHouse evaluates it
// (filters on the time column push down; the verify operator's
// windowed mode tolerates the window edge — its first record's link
// points outside the read and is skipped, its fingerprint recompute is
// not). The stored records come back through the catch-all
// reconstruction: ClickHouse re-sorted the JSON keys, and the
// operators' sort()-canonicalized serialization is what makes the
// recompute match what the archive leg stamped.
every 1h {
  from_clickhouse table="ocsf.API_Activity",
    host="clickhouse-tenzir.tenzir.svc.cluster.local",
    port=9000,
    user="tenzir",
    password=secret("clickhouse-password"),
    tls=false
  where time > now() - 24h
  merge {
    from_clickhouse table="ocsf.Authentication",
      host="clickhouse-tenzir.tenzir.svc.cluster.local",
      port=9000,
      user="tenzir",
      password=secret("clickhouse-password"),
      tls=false
    where time > now() - 24h
  }
  merge {
    from_clickhouse table="ocsf.Account_Change",
      host="clickhouse-tenzir.tenzir.svc.cluster.local",
      port=9000,
      user="tenzir",
      password=secret("clickhouse-password"),
      tls=false
    where time > now() - 24h
  }
  merge {
    from_clickhouse table="ocsf.Detection_Finding",
      host="clickhouse-tenzir.tenzir.svc.cluster.local",
      port=9000,
      user="tenzir",
      password=secret("clickhouse-password"),
      tls=false
    where time > now() - 24h
  }
  merge {
    from_clickhouse table="ocsf.Vulnerability_Finding",
      host="clickhouse-tenzir.tenzir.svc.cluster.local",
      port=9000,
      user="tenzir",
      password=secret("clickhouse-password"),
      tls=false
    where time > now() - 24h
  }
  merge {
    from_clickhouse table="ocsf.Base_Event",
      host="clickhouse-tenzir.tenzir.svc.cluster.local",
      port=9000,
      user="tenzir",
      password=secret("clickhouse-password"),
      tls=false
    where time > now() - 24h
  }
  homelab::record_integrity::verify product="homelab-detection",
    title="Detection record chain break",
    uid_prefix="detection",
    scope_word="chain",
    windowed=true,
    link="stream"
  fork {
    to_stdout { write_json }
  }
  ocsf_derive
  ocsf_cast
  to_clickhouse table="ocsf.Detection_Finding",
    host="clickhouse-tenzir.tenzir.svc.cluster.local",
    port=9000,
    user="tenzir",
    password=secret("clickhouse-password"),
    tls=false,
    mode="append",
    max_batch_rows=65536
}
